<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A histopathologist is a medical doctor who specializes in diagnosing diseases by examining tissues and cells under a microscope. They play a vital role in detecting conditions like cancer, infections, and inflammatory diseases. By analyzing biopsy samples, they provide critical information that helps doctors plan effective treatments. Histopathologists often collaborate closely with surgeons and oncologists, making them key contributors to patient care.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
